SCALE_REALISM: Holds mechanically for the synthetic harness, but realistic workload evidence is insufficient. The packet reports N=300/seed x 7, exact Jaccard plus 64-perm LSH, with FN 1.00 under weak dedup normalizers and 0.00 under aligned NFKC/NFKC+casefold. Missing: real multilingual corpus rate, real tokenizer integration, run through datatrove/text-dedup/NeMo Curator defaults, and demonstrated org-seam evidence.
RATIONALE: I do not find a shipping dedup system that already closes the exact seam by co-locating model tokenizer normalization with MinHash dedup normalization. However, the packet overstates the production baseline if it treats production dedup as raw/NFC-only: datatrove already has configurable text normalization with lowercasing and NFD diacritic stripping, and NeMo Curator ships a separate UnicodeReformatter with NFKC support. Those are partial mitigations, not model-aware alignment. Therefore this is not integration-only, but it is not green until L1 shows the effect survives real pipelines/defaults and quantifies surviving model-identical duplicates at realistic corpus scale.
